Example 1. Computation of Common Logarithms.
To compute common logarithms, the number must be expressed in the form x\cdot10', (1\leq x<10, -\infty\leq q\leq\infty). The common logarithm of x\cdot10' consists of an integral part which is called the characteristic and a decimal part which is called the mantissa. Table 4.1 gives the common logarithm of x.
\[x\quad\quad x\cdot10^{4}\quad\quad\quad\log_{10}x\cdot10^{4}\]
